From e7b12b365277278f4b17b27a23fd2f3219b293be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:56:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] civ45: civics as four policy sliders

Replace the two sliders civ45 inherited from civ54 (Personal Freedom,
Polluting Productivity) with four civics sliders of four steps each:

- Labour (Bronze Working): +5% shields per step, one fewer content
  citizen per two steps.
- Trade (Currency): -5% waste of shields and trade per step, -5% gold.
- Faith (Mysticism): one more content citizen per two steps in cities
  that follow the state faith, -5% science per step.
- Service (Feudalism): one more unit per city free of shield and gold
  upkeep per two steps, one more unhappy citizen per aggressive unit
  per two steps, -5% luxury per step.

Every slider has factor 50, so "per two steps" effects use value 1 and
percentage effects carry twice their per-step value. No minimum_turns:
the server restores a slider to its default whenever it cannot be
changed, and that includes the minimum_turns lockout.

The three training-duration sliders stay.
